+# FIX-140 — confirmed initial wallet-symbol retry and audited historical retirement
+
+Status: REVIEW CANDIDATE. Java 21 compilation, Maven/JUnit, and real MySQL validation have not run. This workspace has a Java 17 JRE and no javac, Maven, or MySQL. JavaScript syntax check passed. Do not interpret source inspection as a successful build.
+
+## Implemented scope
+
+A shared signal's first wallet-symbol SELECT FOR UPDATE may schedule a retry only when a private marker proves the failure occurred at that call, the exception is a recognized lock timeout/deadlock, and Spring afterCompletion reported ROLLED_BACK. SQLState 08 communications failures do not qualify. Business/commit failures retain review behavior.
+
+The existing shared LIVE dispatcher resumes the exact registered signal. It owns all attempts; SignalProcessingRecovery remains deferred in shared mode. Retry delays are 1/3/10 seconds, with four total attempts; there is no sleep and no held connection during the delay. The existing latest-candle/freshness gate runs after lock acquisition on retries. Expired attempts map to EXECUTION_EXPIRED; exhausted proven non-executions map to EXECUTION_NOT_EXECUTED. No signal regeneration or wallet replay is granted by an Optional.empty result. Persistence uncertainty retains review.
+
+Work state SYMBOL_LOCK_RETRY with failure_stage INITIAL_SYMBOL_LOCK_ROLLED_BACK is new evidence, not a reinterpretation of old QueryTimeoutException strings. Generic REVIEW_REQUIRED records cannot enter this path. A crash between work persistence and delivery persistence remains review-only; automatic incident reconciliation is not implemented.
+
+Initial-position deadlock behavior remains the existing two-attempt policy. Protection failures in ENA/ICP/SUI are not automatically repaired by this patch. Existing incident records require separate evidence-based reconciliation.
+
+## Historical queue handling
+
+No DELETE statement is introduced. Source candles, existing trade_signal rows, wallet records, and consumer checkpoints are retained. An opt-in worker retires only untouched expired phase-4 PENDING/HISTORICAL_DEFERRED analysis rows, with absent analysis start/completion markers and no processing/wallet or incomplete-protection evidence. It records HISTORICAL_SKIPPED, retirement time, reason and operation identity; it does not fabricate analysis_completed_at.
+
+Owner tokens retained from the price phase are not analysis claims. Eligibility is rechecked under symbol-state then delivery-row locks. Active analysis is excluded by status and attempt markers. Keyset scan progress avoids repeatedly encountering ineligible queue heads; it is advisory and resets when exhausted. Each tick scans one symbol/interval lane, at most 20 candidates, with independent three-second mutation transactions. V95 supplies the lane selection index; inspect EXPLAIN on the target MySQL server before enabling writes.
+
+Compatibility defaults:
+- shared-market.analysis.historical-enabled=true
+- shared-market.analysis.retirement-enabled=false
+- shared-market.analysis.retirement-dry-run=true
+- shared-market.analysis.retirement-retain-seconds=172800
+- shared-market.analysis.retirement-delay-ms=5000
+
+Explicit dry-run of all untouched expired queue history:
+```
+--shared-market.analysis.historical-enabled=false
+--shared-market.analysis.retirement-enabled=true
+--shared-market.analysis.retirement-dry-run=true
+--shared-market.analysis.retirement-retain-seconds=0
+```
+After reviewing dry-run evidence, changing retirement-dry-run to false enables mutation. Zero extra retention never retires a still-live close. RUNNING, REVIEW_REQUIRED, previously attempted, processing-attributed, or unresolved protection rows are not retired. Retiring every database history record is intentionally not provided.
+
+Disabling historical recovery can remove future reconstruction of missing decision context. This is not proven neutral for live trading. Existing saved context is retained, but keeping stored signals does not prove missing inputs are adequately covered. Consumers include MTF, same-interval BTC, position protection, opportunity consolidation, execution intelligence and validation. Bounded context restoration and Production/Replay context-window acceptance are NOT implemented here. History therefore remains enabled by default.
+
+## Observability
+
+FIX-125 LOCK_ACQUIRE_FAILED complements existing LOCK_WAIT/TX_COMPLETED. Transaction completion distinguishes UNKNOWN from ROLLED_BACK. FIX-140 SAFE_RETRY_RESULT correlates event/signal/attempt/outcome with confirmed rollback. Context evaluation counters count every MTF FULL/PARTIAL/MISSING and BTC present/missing lookup; summaries are rate-limited, the underlying counts are not. They do not change decisions. BTC coverage does not establish freshness and LEARNING early returns are not counted as saved-signal lookups. No dashboard health wiring or throughput claim is included.
+
+## Validation required
+
+Five new H2 coordinator tests cover due-time enforcement, exact-signal resumption, expiry, later business timeout, four-attempt exhaustion, and communications classification (five test methods; first method covers several assertions). Six retirement tests cover audited retirement, processing evidence, incomplete protection, dry-run, history-enabled guard and fresh-close retention. Existing expired-signal test now permits the bounded attributed-retry lookup while continuing to prohibit wallet processing.
+
+Before deployment run the complete Java 21 Maven suite and real MySQL ownership/rollback/claim/rejection/expiry tests. Add two-instance resume, uncertain rollback, crash between state commits, late completion, and actual MySQL EXPLAIN/load acceptance. Production/Replay scoring functions are unchanged; scheduling/actual execution availability changes and is not claimed parity-validated.
+
+## Explicit remaining work
+
+Protection-specific safe recovery; existing-incident reconciliation; cross-instance failure-injection acceptance; graceful deployment/shutdown fencing; bounded missing-context restoration; stale-context/dashboard metrics. No worker or DB-pool count increase. The current ZIP did not include the current Jenkinsfile/Deploy-Trader script, so no deployment-script modification is bundled.
+
+## Review follow-up: dispatcher and worker coverage
+
+SharedMarketConsumerTest now drives real dispatcher, real worker, real registration store and real coordinator through a controlled initial symbol-lock timeout, persisted due-time propagation, a not-due negative control, actual waiting for the original persisted deadline, exact-signal resumption, one business commit, and duplicate-dispatch suppression. It asserts zero historical executor submissions and only one scoring/indicator pass. Freshness policy is controlled in this orchestration test; coordinator expiry tests exercise its SQL-backed gate separately.
+
+The due-time propagation now uses a guarded single-row read and update in the same delivery transaction instead of a MySQL-only join update, so the actual SQL path is exercised on H2. Missing or ambiguous work aborts the transaction. Worker parameterized tests cover COMPLETED, EXPIRED, LOCK_RETRY_EXHAUSTED, SYMBOL_LOCK_RETRY and REVIEW_REQUIRED mappings on its saved-signal resumption branch. These new tests are authored but not executed here; Java21/Maven/MySQL tooling remains unavailable. This closes authored coverage, not runtime acceptance.
+
+## Jenkins validation follow-up
+
+The supplied Java 21 Jenkins run compiled successfully and executed 407 tests: two failures, zero errors. SharedMarketConsumerTest passed all 40 tests. Both failures were the existing fresh-redelivery tests rejecting the new attributed-retry lookup as an unverified Mockito interaction. Their helper now explicitly stubs an empty retry result and verifies the exact SQL and event ID before checking completed-work evidence, preserving verifyNoMoreInteractions and no wallet/scoring interactions. Production code is unchanged by this correction. The corrected full suite must be rerun; no green build or real MySQL acceptance is claimed.
